    {
      "data": {
        "text": "<thinking> To create the Python file `validate_document_fields.py` that validates required structured fields and confidence scores using an external provider, I will select Amazon Textract as the concrete external provider. Amazon Textract is a service that automatically extracts text and data from scanned documents. It will be identifiable in the code through the use of the `boto3` library, which is the Amazon Web Services (AWS) SDK for Python, and the specific calls to the Textract service. </thinking>\n",
        "time": {
          "end": 1789860553900,
          "start": 1789860549645
        },
        "type": "text"
      },
      "id": "prt_0bc00940d0013ZCB6cjqAvFWJe",
      "message_id": "msg_0bc008fea001RB9t9nzqv8nJb1",
      "session_id": "ses_f43ff7027ffeWRuwDPHag2Zi33",
